  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🕰️ Vintage Shop Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a vintage, thrift or antique shop, from Thrift Happens to The Old Forge Emporium."
    },
    "intro": "Good vintage shop names hint at a past life (<em>Then Again Vintage</em>), a decade (<em>Sixties Archive</em>) or a find (<em>Dust &amp; Gold</em>), and they're easy to say when someone tells a friend where they got their jacket. Opening a vintage clothing rail, a thrift store, an antiques centre or a secondhand homeware shop? This **vintage shop name generator** gives you names in eight styles, from thrift puns to proper antique shop names, and you can check each one is free before you paint the sign.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good vintage shop names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>Then Again Vintage</strong>: a gentle nod to clothes having a second life.</li><li><strong>Retro Active</strong>: a pun that also says the shop is lively.</li><li><strong>Sixties Archive</strong>: names the decade, so collectors know what to expect.</li><li><strong>Chintz &amp; Chrome</strong>: two eras in three words: floral fabric and diner chrome.</li><li><strong>Dust &amp; Gold</strong>: the promise of every rummage: most of it's dust, some of it's gold.</li><li><strong>Lot 73 Vintage</strong>: borrows the language of auction lots.</li><li><strong>Cartwright Vintage &amp; Retro</strong>: a family name for a shop that wants to feel established.</li><li><strong>Thrifty Business</strong>: a pun that suits a charity-style or budget rail.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Vintage, antique, retro or thrift?",
        "content": "<p>The words mean different things to customers, so pick the one that matches your stock:</p><ul><li><strong>Vintage</strong> is usually used for things at least 20 years old, especially clothes.</li><li><strong>Antique</strong> is usually kept for things around 100 years old or more. These are common trade usages, not legal definitions.</li><li><strong>Retro</strong> means new things made in an old style, or a look borrowed from a past decade.</li><li><strong>Thrift, preloved and secondhand</strong> say it's affordable rather than collectable. \"Thrift store\" is US wording; in the UK people say charity shop or secondhand shop.</li></ul><p>Choose <strong>Classic antiques</strong> for an emporium or antiques centre, <strong>Thrift and resale</strong> for a budget rail, and <strong>For Instagram</strong> if you sell mostly online.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you paint the sign",
        "content": "<p>Before you pay for a sign, a logo or printed bags, check the name is free:</p><ul><li><strong>Company register:</strong> if you form a limited company in the UK, Companies House won't accept a name that's the same as one already registered. In the US, search your state's business register.</li><li><strong>Trade marks:</strong> search the UK IPO or USPTO register for your kind of goods, so you don't clash with an existing brand.</li><li><strong>Web and social:</strong> check the domain and the handles you'll use, since many customers will find you on Instagram first.</li></ul><p>Press <strong>Check</strong> on any name, or use the <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a>, to run those searches in one place. The <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a> guide covers the rest. This is general guidance, not legal advice.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Making the name work in the shop",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Say the era if you specialise.</strong> A shop that only sells 1960s and 70s clothes is easier to find if the name says so.</li><li><strong>Think about the swing tag.</strong> Short names fit labels and carrier bags.</li><li><strong>Selling online too?</strong> Check the name works as a handle without spaces.</li></ul><p>For new handmade stock, try the <a href=\"etsy-shop-name-generator.html\">Etsy Shop</a> and <a href=\"sewing-business-name-generator.html\">Sewing Business</a> name generators; for a mixed shop, the <a href=\"gift-shop-name-generator.html\">Gift Shop Name Generator</a> and <a href=\"boutique-name-generator.html\">Boutique Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_shops-names.html\">shop and brand business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
