        "question": "What is a good name for a thrift store?",
        "answer": "One that tells people they will find secondhand treasure, is easy to say and still fits a handle. Puns on second, twice and past (<em>Thrift Happens</em>, <em>Worn Again</em>) suit a clothing rail or an Instagram shop; an antiques centre does better with a classic name such as <em>The Old Forge Emporium</em>. Avoid names close to big resale chains and charities, such as Goodwill, Oxfam or Beyond Retro."
